	)
	(text "U4 DRAM controller + 72-pin SIMM (spec 3.2, 4.3, 5)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "42816930-393e-5c25-a136-83afe92f7c51")
	)
	(text "FITTED PINOUT: Yosys + hoglet67/atf15xx_yosys -> Microchip fit1508.exe v1918 (Wine), ATF1508AS PLCC84 -7, JTAG ON,\npins locked (-preassign keep), -optimize on, -pin_keep on. Result: 80/128 macrocells, 52 flip-flops, 210 product terms;\n55/60 user I/O + 4 JTAG + 3/4 dedicated inputs. Worst register-to-register 14.0 ns (50 MHz = 20 ns met).\nSources, reports, JEDEC, testbench: cpld/dram/ (dram.v, dram.fit, dram.jed, timing.txt, sim/).\nLogic after Mackerel-30 dram_controller.v (C. Maykish, MIT): 50 MHz FSM, 2-flop AS synchroniser, CBR refresh\nevery 7.5 us alternating sides, 100 us + 16 CBR power-up, CAS lanes from SIZ1/SIZ0/A1/A0, DSACK1+0 (32-bit port).\nPins 16/17/18/50 (STERM_n/CBREQ_n/CBACK_n/DS_n) are unused in Rev A: reached only through open solder jumpers.\nPin 2 (GCLK2) carries CLK_DRAMC for a future CPU-synchronous (burst) FSM; pin 81 spare -> TP809."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d775088f-0f7c-514f-b40e-a619224da4b0")
	)
	(text "Series resistors: 33R source termination on MA/RAS/CAS/WE. Trace Z0 ~50-60R minus the CPLD output impedance\n(~15-25R) [EST]; SIMM input loads (Micron): MA 48/95 pF, WE 64/127 pF, RAS 32 pF, CAS 16/32 pF (1/2-sided) ->\n33R x 100 pF ~ 3.3 ns edge slowing, inside the DRAM timing margins (tRAH/tASC/tCAH >= 14 ns post-fit)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9985ea9f-dbd3-5bb9-9492-94a995ab2b43")
	)
